{
  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "t98",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "swapi answers /people?search=sky with a redirect to /people/?search=sky: every read of it is two requests. The ingest writes the address it was given, `characters live at \\\"/people\\\"`; it could write ",
      "excerpt": "swapi answers /people?search=sky with a redirect to /people/?search=sky: every read of it is two requests. The ingest writes the address it was given, `characters live at \\\"/people\\\"`; it could write ",
      "text": "This should be noted in the .api.spell somehow",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T02:06:34.724Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T02:13:40.264Z",
          "html": "<p>Agreed, and the fix is the note: the ingest will write the address swapi answers at, with its slash, so the file shows it plainly:</p>\n<pre><code>- characters live at \"/people/\"</code></pre>\n<p>When a server redirects, the ingest follows it once while it looks, writes the address it landed on, and says so in its report (\"swapi moves /people to /people/: wrote the second\").  Every read is then one request, not two.  <code>spell place update</code> does the same for a file written before.  Going into P27 now.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T02:13:37.872Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "t105",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "P27: spell place update adds every collection a server lists (up to 12), not the ones the ingest was asked for: PokéAPI's file grows by berries, contest effects ... -- remember --collections in the de",
      "excerpt": "P27: spell place update adds every collection a server lists (up to 12), not the ones the ingest was asked for: PokéAPI's file grows by berries, contest effects ... -- remember --collections in the de",
      "text": "It is not at all clear what this means.  Sounds like I don't care, though, just fix it",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T02:12:16.428Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T02:13:41.090Z",
          "html": "<p>Fixing it.  In short:  you ask the ingest for 7 of PokéAPI's collections; a later <code>spell place update</code> forgot that and added every collection the server lists, so the file grew berries and contest effects you never asked for.  The fix:  the description remembers which collections you asked for, and an update looks again at only those.  Going into P27 now.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T02:13:38.720Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "t106",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "P27: a collection found by name can't be read as a list: every wiki page answers an error at its address with no name -- say so at compile time",
      "excerpt": "P27: a collection found by name can't be read as a list: every wiki page answers an error at its address with no name -- say so at compile time",
      "text": "details please",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T02:12:35.085Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T02:13:41.884Z",
          "html": "<p>Wikipedia's pages can only be found by name:  <code>/page/summary/Luke_Skywalker</code> answers one page, but there's no address that lists every page.  So in Spell:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>the wiki page named \"Luke Skywalker\"</code> works:  one read, by name.</li>\n<li><code>every wiki page</code>, or <code>&lt;for wiki pages&gt;</code>, can't work:  Spell would ask <code>/page/summary/</code> with no name, and Wikipedia answers an error.  Today that only shows when the program runs, as a failed read.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The fix:  a collection whose rows are found by name says so (the ingest writes <code>wiki pages are found at \"/page/summary/{name}\"</code>), and the compiler refuses a read of all of them with a message that says what to write instead:</p>\n<pre><code>wiki pages are only found by name:  write \"the wiki page named ...\" </code></pre>\n<p>Going into P27 now.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T02:13:39.477Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
